#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Ali was told to stay behind until he had returned the deposits people had left with the Prophet ﷺ."
msgstr "‘Ali diminta untuk tetap tinggal sehingga beliau memulangkan barang-barang amanah yang dititipkan orang ramai kepada Nabi ﷺ."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The searchers came so close that Abu Bakr whispered, “If one of them looked down at his feet, he would see us.” The Prophet ﷺ answered, “What do you think of two, when Allah is their third?”"
msgstr "Orang-orang yang mencari itu menghampiri begitu dekat sehingga Abu Bakr berbisik, “Jika salah seorang daripada mereka melihat ke bawah kakinya, dia pasti melihat kita.” Nabi ﷺ menjawab, “Apakah sangkaanmu terhadap dua orang, sedangkan Allah menjadi yang ketiga bersama mereka?”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Allah recalled this moment in the Quran: “the second of two, when they were in the cave, when he said to his companion, ‘Do not grieve; Allah is with us.’”"
msgstr "Allah merakam detik ini di dalam al-Quran: “salah seorang daripada dua orang semasa mereka berdua berada di dalam gua, ketika dia berkata kepada sahabatnya, ‘Janganlah berduka cita; sesungguhnya Allah bersama kita.’”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "In Ibn Ishaq’s telling, when the three nights had passed, Asma brought their food but had no strap to hang the bag. She undid her waist-belt and tied it on, and so she was called She of the Two Belts."
msgstr "Menurut riwayat Ibn Ishaq, setelah tiga malam berlalu, Asma membawa makanan mereka tetapi tiada tali pengikat untuk menggantung beg itu. Dia membuka tali pinggangnya lalu mengikatkannya, dan oleh sebab itu dia digelar Wanita Berikat Pinggang Dua."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The pursuers climbed the mountain and passed the cave. Seeing a spider’s web across its opening, they said no one could have gone in there, and moved on. Ibn Kathir calls this report’s chain good."
msgstr "Para pengejar mendaki gunung itu dan melepasi gua tersebut. Melihat sarang labah-labah merentangi pintu gua, mereka berkata tiada sesiapa yang mungkin memasukinya, lalu beredar. Ibn Kathir menilai sanad riwayat ini sebagai baik."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Some tell that the searchers saw a spider’s web across the cave’s opening, and walked on."
msgstr "Ada yang meriwayatkan bahawa orang-orang yang mencari itu melihat sarang labah-labah merentangi pintu gua, lalu berlalu pergi."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Al-Bukhari gives three nights. Which nights of the week they were comes from a later biography."
msgstr "Al-Bukhari menyebut tiga malam. Hari-hari yang dimaksudkan dalam seminggu itu diperoleh daripada karya sirah yang terkemudian."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah tells how the two reached a cave on Mount Thawr and hid there for three nights."
msgstr "‘Aishah menceritakan bagaimana mereka berdua tiba di sebuah gua di Gunung Thawr dan bersembunyi di situ selama tiga malam."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah tells how her brother ‘Abdullah spent the nights with them and brought them news from Makkah after dark."
msgstr "‘Aishah menceritakan bagaimana saudaranya ‘Abdullah bermalam bersama mereka dan membawa berita dari Makkah selepas gelap malam."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Aishah tells how ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah brought the ewes to the cave each evening of the three nights."
msgstr "‘Aishah menceritakan bagaimana ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah membawa kambing-kambing betina itu ke gua setiap petang sepanjang tiga malam tersebut."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr recalls fearing that anyone who looked down at his own feet would see them."
msgstr "Abu Bakr mengenang rasa bimbangnya bahawa sesiapa sahaja yang melihat ke bawah kakinya sendiri pasti akan melihat mereka."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The verse speaks of the Prophet ﷺ as the second of two in the cave, telling his companion not to grieve."
msgstr "Ayat tersebut menyebut tentang Nabi ﷺ sebagai salah seorang daripada dua orang di dalam gua, yang memberitahu sahabatnya agar tidak berdukacita."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Kathir explains the verse: Allah supported and aided His Messenger, who sheltered in the cave for three days."
msgstr "Ibn Kathir menjelaskan ayat tersebut: Allah menyokong dan menolong Rasul-Nya, yang berlindung di dalam gua selama tiga hari."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Ibn Ishaq tells how Asma tied the food bag with her waist-belt, and so was called She of the Two Belts."
msgstr "Ibn Ishaq menceritakan bagaimana Asma mengikat beg makanan dengan tali pinggangnya, dan oleh sebab itu digelar Wanita Berikat Pinggang Dua."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The report of the spider’s web across the cave’s opening, whose chain Ibn Kathir calls good."
msgstr "Riwayat mengenai sarang labah-labah yang merentangi pintu gua, yang sanadnya dinilai baik oleh Ibn Kathir."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "A modern biography names the three nights: the nights before Friday, Saturday and Sunday."
msgstr "Sebuah karya sirah moden menamakan tiga malam tersebut: malam menjelang Jumaat, Sabtu dan Ahad."

#: src/routes/Journey.svelte
msgid "The number beside each book counts its source passages."
msgstr "Nombor di sebelah setiap kitab ialah bilangan petikan sumbernya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr reached a cave on Mount Thawr and hid inside it. They would stay there for three nights."
msgstr "Nabi ﷺ dan Abu Bakr tiba di sebuah gua di Bukit Thawr lalu bersembunyi di dalamnya. Mereka tinggal di situ selama tiga malam."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Each night, Abu Bakr’s son ‘Abdullah slept near them. Before dawn he slipped back to Makkah, so that morning found him among Quraysh as if he had never left, and at dark he returned with any plot he had heard."
msgstr "Setiap malam, anak lelaki Abu Bakr, ‘Abdullah, tidur berdekatan mereka. Sebelum subuh, dia menyelinap pulang ke Makkah, agar apabila pagi tiba dia sudah berada dalam kalangan Quraysh seolah-olah tidak pernah pergi, dan setelah malam dia kembali membawa sebarang rancangan yang didengarinya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr’s freedman ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah grazed a few milking ewes nearby and brought them to the cave after nightfall, so the two had milk. He did this on each of the three nights."
msgstr "Bekas hamba Abu Bakr, ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah, menggembala beberapa ekor kambing perah berhampiran situ dan membawanya ke gua setelah malam tiba, agar mereka berdua mendapat bekalan susu. Dia melakukan hal ini pada setiap malam sepanjang tiga malam tersebut."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr slipped into a cave on Mount Thawr and stayed out of sight. For three nights, it would be their hiding place."
msgstr "Nabi ﷺ dan Abu Bakr menyelinap masuk ke dalam sebuah gua di Gunung Thawr lalu bersembunyi. Selama tiga malam, gua itu menjadi tempat persembunyian mereka."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "They were not alone for long. Each night Abu Bakr’s son ‘Abdullah came after dark with whatever Quraysh were plotting, then slipped back before dawn, so that morning found him in Makkah as if he had never left."
msgstr "Mereka tidak lama bersendirian. Setiap malam, anak Abu Bakr, ‘Abdullah, datang selepas hari gelap untuk menyampaikan apa sahaja rancangan Quraysh, kemudian menyelinap pulang sebelum fajar. Apabila pagi tiba, dia sudah berada di Makkah seolah-olah tidak pernah pergi."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "And as darkness settled, Abu Bakr’s freedman ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah brought a few milking ewes to the cave, so the two had fresh milk. Every one of the three nights, he came."
msgstr "Apabila malam menjelang, hamba yang telah dimerdekakan oleh Abu Bakr, ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah, membawa beberapa ekor biri-biri betina yang boleh diperah susunya ke gua itu, supaya mereka berdua mendapat susu segar. Dia datang pada setiap malam selama tiga malam itu."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Then the searchers came close, so close that Abu Bakr whispered, “If one of them looked down at his feet, he would see us.” The Prophet ﷺ answered, “What do you think of two, when Allah is their third?”"
msgstr "Kemudian para pencari itu datang begitu dekat sehingga Abu Bakr berbisik, “Jika salah seorang daripada mereka melihat ke bawah, ke arah kakinya, dia pasti nampak kita.” Nabi ﷺ menjawab, “Apakah sangkaanmu tentang dua orang yang Allah menjadi yang ketiga bersama mereka?”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Allah preserved that moment in the Quran: “the second of two, when they were in the cave, when he said to his companion, ‘Do not grieve; Allah is with us.’”"
msgstr "Allah mengabadikan peristiwa itu dalam al-Quran: “orang yang kedua daripada dua orang, ketika mereka berada di dalam gua, ketika dia berkata kepada sahabatnya, ‘Janganlah bersedih; sesungguhnya Allah bersama kita.’”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Late that night the Prophet ﷺ left his house and set out with Abu Bakr, who carried all his savings with him. They did not take the road north to Madinah, but turned south, towards Yemen."
msgstr "Lewat malam itu, Nabi ﷺ meninggalkan rumahnya dan berangkat bersama Abu Bakr, yang membawa semua wang simpanannya. Mereka tidak mengambil jalan ke utara menuju Madinah, sebaliknya menuju ke selatan, ke arah Yaman."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "That night, the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr quietly left Makkah. They went south, the opposite way to Madinah."
msgstr "Malam itu, Nabi ﷺ dan Abu Bakr meninggalkan Makkah dengan senyap-senyap. Mereka menuju ke selatan, bertentangan arah dengan Madinah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "About five miles on, they reached Mount Thawr. They climbed to a cave in its side and slipped inside, out of sight. For three nights, it would be their hiding place."
msgstr "Kira-kira lima batu perjalanan, mereka tiba di Gunung Thawr. Mereka mendaki ke sebuah gua di lerengnya lalu masuk ke dalam tanpa dilihat orang. Gua itu menjadi tempat persembunyian mereka selama tiga malam."

