#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Each year more came, until seventy-three men and two women met him there by night and pledged to protect him as they protected their own women and children. “I am of you and you are of me,” he said."
msgstr "Setiap tahun, semakin ramai yang datang, sehingga tujuh puluh tiga lelaki dan dua wanita bertemu dengannya di sana pada waktu malam. Mereka berjanji akan melindunginya seperti mereka melindungi wanita dan anak-anak mereka sendiri. “Aku bersama kamu, dan kamu bersamaku,” katanya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Later, many more came at night. They promised to keep him safe, just like their own families."
msgstr "Kemudian, ramai lagi datang pada waktu malam. Mereka berjanji akan melindunginya seperti keluarga mereka sendiri."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "“It is Yathrib,” he told his companions, and group after group they slipped away to Madinah. At last, of those free to go, only he, Abu Bakr and ‘Ali were left. And he waited for Allah’s permission to follow."
msgstr "“Pergilah ke Yathrib,” katanya kepada para sahabatnya. Mereka pun berangkat ke Madinah sedikit demi sedikit. Akhirnya, antara mereka yang bebas untuk pergi, hanya beliau, Abu Bakr dan ‘Ali yang masih tinggal. Beliau menunggu izin Allah untuk menyusul."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "So his friends moved to Yathrib, the town we call Madinah. The Prophet ﷺ waited for Allah’s permission to follow."
msgstr "Maka para sahabatnya berpindah ke Yathrib, kota yang kita kenali sebagai Madinah. Nabi ﷺ menunggu izin Allah untuk menyusul."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr asked again and again to go. “Do not hurry,” he was told. “Perhaps Allah will give you a companion.” So he waited, hoping it would be the Prophet ﷺ, and fed two camels for four months to have them ready."
msgstr "Abu Bakr berkali-kali meminta izin untuk pergi. “Jangan terburu-buru,” katanya kepadanya. “Barangkali Allah akan memberimu seorang teman.” Maka dia menunggu, berharap teman itu ialah Nabi ﷺ, sambil memberi makan dua ekor unta selama empat bulan agar kedua-duanya bersedia."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Abu Bakr wanted to go too. He was told to wait: perhaps Allah would give him a companion."
msgstr "Abu Bakr juga ingin pergi. Dia diminta menunggu: barangkali Allah akan memberinya seorang teman."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Then one day, in the full heat of noon, the Prophet ﷺ came at an hour he never came, and said, “Allah has given me permission to leave.” “Companionship?” Abu Bakr asked. “Companionship.” And Abu Bakr wept for joy."
msgstr "Kemudian pada suatu hari, ketika tengah hari panas terik, Nabi ﷺ datang pada waktu yang luar biasa baginya lalu berkata, “Allah telah mengizinkan aku berangkat.” “Bolehkah aku menemanimu?” tanya Abu Bakr. “Ya, temani aku.” Abu Bakr pun menangis kegembiraan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "One hot noon, the Prophet ﷺ came with the news: they could go together! Abu Bakr cried for joy."
msgstr "Pada suatu tengah hari yang panas, Nabi ﷺ membawa berita: mereka boleh berangkat bersama! Abu Bakr menangis kegembiraan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "They hired a guide to bring the camels to the cave of Thawr after three nights. Abu Bakr’s daughter Asma had nothing to tie up their food, so she split her waistband in two, and became “she of the two waistbands”."
msgstr "Mereka mengupah seorang penunjuk jalan untuk membawa unta ke gua Thawr selepas tiga malam. Asma, anak perempuan Abu Bakr, tidak mempunyai apa-apa untuk mengikat bekalan makanan mereka. Jadi, dia membelah tali pinggangnya menjadi dua, lalu dikenali sebagai “wanita yang mempunyai dua tali pinggang”."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Asma had nothing to tie up their food, so she split her waistband in two and used that."
msgstr "Asma tiada apa-apa untuk mengikat bekalan makanan mereka, jadi dia membelah tali pinggangnya menjadi dua dan menggunakannya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "In Makkah, Quraysh had watched his companions go, and feared he would follow. In Dar al-Nadwah their leaders took Abu Jahl’s plan: young men from every clan would strike him together, spreading his blood across them all."
msgstr "Di Makkah, Quraysh melihat para sahabat Nabi berangkat dan bimbang beliau akan menyusul. Di Dar al-Nadwah, para pemimpin mereka menerima rancangan Abu Jahl: pemuda daripada setiap kabilah akan menyerangnya serentak, supaya darahnya tertanggung oleh semua kabilah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The leaders of Makkah were afraid of the Prophet ﷺ, and they made a plan to attack him."
msgstr "Para pemimpin Makkah takut akan Nabi ﷺ lalu merancang untuk menyerangnya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "That night the men gathered at his door, waiting for him to sleep. He told ‘Ali to lie in his bed, wrapped in his green cloak. “Sleep in it,” he said. “Nothing you dislike will reach you from them.”"
msgstr "Pada malam itu, para lelaki berkumpul di depan pintunya, menunggu sehingga beliau tidur. Beliau menyuruh ‘Ali berbaring di tempat tidurnya, berselimutkan jubah hijau beliau. “Tidurlah di situ,” katanya. “Tiada apa-apa yang kamu tidak sukai daripada mereka akan menimpamu.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "That night they waited outside his door. ‘Ali lay in the Prophet’s bed, wrapped in his green cloak."
msgstr "Pada malam itu, mereka menunggu di luar pintunya. ‘Ali berbaring di tempat tidur Nabi, berselimutkan jubah hijau beliau."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Then he came out to them with a handful of dust, scattering it over their heads and reciting, “So We have covered them, and they do not see.” Allah took their sight from him, and he went on his way."
msgstr "Kemudian beliau keluar menemui mereka dengan segenggam tanah, lalu menaburkannya ke atas kepala mereka sambil membaca, “Lalu Kami tutup pandangan mereka, sehingga mereka tidak dapat melihat.” Allah menghalang mereka daripada melihat beliau, lalu beliau meneruskan perjalanannya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The Prophet ﷺ walked right out past them, scattering dust, and Allah kept them from seeing him."
msgstr "Nabi ﷺ berjalan keluar melewati mereka sambil menaburkan tanah, dan Allah menghalang mereka daripada melihatnya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He came to Abu Bakr, and the two slipped out by a small door at the back of the house, Abu Bakr carrying all his savings. They did not take the road north to Madinah, but turned south, towards Yemen."
msgstr "Beliau pergi menemui Abu Bakr, lalu mereka berdua menyelinap keluar melalui sebuah pintu kecil di belakang rumah. Abu Bakr membawa semua wang simpanannya. Mereka tidak mengambil jalan ke utara menuju Madinah, sebaliknya menuju ke selatan, ke arah Yaman."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He and his best friend, Abu Bakr, slipped away in the dark. They went south, the opposite way to Madinah."
msgstr "Beliau dan sahabat karibnya, Abu Bakr, menyelinap pergi dalam gelap. Mereka bergerak ke selatan, bertentangan arah dengan Madinah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "About five miles on, they reached Mount Thawr and a cave in its side. Abu Bakr went in first, feeling his way in the dark, ready to take any harm himself. For three nights, it would be their hiding place."
msgstr "Selepas menempuh kira-kira lima batu, mereka sampai ke Gunung Thawr dan sebuah gua di lerengnya. Abu Bakr masuk dahulu, meraba-raba dalam gelap dan bersedia menanggung sendiri apa-apa bahaya. Gua itu akan menjadi tempat persembunyian mereka selama tiga malam."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "They reached a cave on Mount Thawr. Abu Bakr went in first to make sure it was safe."
msgstr "Mereka tiba di sebuah gua di Gunung Thawr. Abu Bakr masuk dahulu untuk memastikan tempat itu selamat."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "As darkness settled, Abu Bakr’s freedman ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah brought his milking sheep to the cave, so the two had fresh milk. At dawn he drove the flock along ‘Abdullah’s trail, and the sheep wiped out his footprints."
msgstr "Apabila malam menjelang, ‘Amir ibn Fuhayrah, bekas hamba Abu Bakr yang telah dimerdekakan, membawa biri-biri susunya ke gua supaya mereka berdua mendapat susu segar. Ketika fajar, dia menggiring kawanan itu melalui jejak ‘Abdullah, lalu biri-biri tersebut menghapuskan kesan tapak kakinya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "‘Amir brought sheep every evening for milk. In the morning, the sheep walked over ‘Abdullah’s footprints."
msgstr "Setiap petang, ‘Amir membawa biri-biri agar mereka mendapat susu. Pada waktu pagi, biri-biri itu berjalan di atas jejak tapak kaki ‘Abdullah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Searchers stood right above the cave! Abu Bakr was afraid they would look down. The Prophet ﷺ calmed his friend."
msgstr "Para pencari berada betul-betul di atas gua! Abu Bakr takut mereka akan menjenguk ke bawah. Nabi ﷺ menenangkan sahabatnya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Then the guide came with the camels, as arranged, and now there were four of them, with ‘Amir riding behind Abu Bakr. The guide led them down below Makkah and out along the coast, “by the edge of the sea.”"
msgstr "Kemudian penunjuk jalan datang membawa unta seperti yang dijanjikan. Kini ada empat ekor unta, dengan ‘Amir menunggang di belakang Abu Bakr. Penunjuk jalan membawa mereka turun ke bawah Makkah dan menyusuri pesisir, “di tepi laut.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "After three nights, their guide came with the camels, and they rode out along the coast by the sea."
msgstr "Selepas tiga malam, penunjuk jalan mereka datang membawa unta, lalu mereka menunggang menyusuri pesisir laut."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "People on the road knew Abu Bakr, but not the man with him. “Who is this man in front of you?” they asked. “This man guides me on the way,” he answered. They thought he meant the road; he meant the way of good."
msgstr "Orang yang ditemui di jalan mengenali Abu Bakr, tetapi tidak mengenali lelaki yang bersamanya. “Siapakah lelaki di hadapanmu ini?” tanya mereka. “Dia membimbingku dalam perjalanan,” jawab Abu Bakr. Mereka menyangka Abu Bakr maksudkan jalan yang dilalui; sebenarnya dia maksudkan jalan kebaikan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "People asked Abu Bakr who was with him. “He guides me on the way,” he said: the way of good."
msgstr "Orang bertanya kepada Abu Bakr siapa yang bersamanya. “Dia membimbingku di jalan,” jawabnya—jalan kebaikan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Quraysh had put a price on the two. A man told Suraqah ibn Malik he had seen dark figures by the coast. “I knew that it was them,” Suraqah said, but he told the man otherwise. He wanted the hundred camels for himself."
msgstr "Quraysh menawarkan ganjaran untuk menangkap mereka berdua. Seorang lelaki memberitahu Suraqah ibn Malik bahawa dia ternampak beberapa susuk tubuh di pesisir. “Aku tahu itu mereka,” kata Suraqah, tetapi dia memberitahu lelaki itu sebaliknya. Dia mahu mendapatkan seratus ekor unta itu untuk dirinya sendiri."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "On the road by the sea, a rider called Suraqah raced after them on his horse, hoping for a big reward."
msgstr "Di jalan tepi laut, seorang penunggang bernama Suraqah mengejar mereka dengan kudanya, mengharapkan ganjaran besar."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He rode hard until he could hear the Prophet ﷺ reciting. The Prophet ﷺ did not look back; Abu Bakr kept looking back. Then his horse’s forelegs sank into the ground up to the knees, and Suraqah fell."
msgstr "Dia menunggang sepantas mungkin sehingga dapat mendengar Rasulullah ﷺ membaca. Rasulullah ﷺ tidak menoleh, tetapi Abu Bakr kerap menoleh ke belakang. Tiba-tiba kaki hadapan kudanya terbenam ke dalam tanah hingga ke lutut, lalu Suraqah terjatuh."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Suraqah called out for safety and offered them provisions. They asked only, “Keep our whereabouts hidden.” ‘Amir wrote him a letter of safety on leather, and Suraqah rode back, turning every pursuer home."
msgstr "Suraqah meminta jaminan keselamatan dan menawarkan bekalan kepada mereka. Mereka hanya meminta, “Rahsiakan tempat kami.” ‘Amir menulis surat jaminan keselamatan untuknya pada sekeping kulit, lalu Suraqah menunggang pulang dan menyuruh setiap orang yang mengejar mereka pulang."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Suraqah gave up the chase. They asked him only to keep their secret, and he sent the other riders home."
msgstr "Suraqah menghentikan pengejarannya. Mereka hanya memintanya merahsiakan keberadaan mereka, lalu dia menyuruh penunggang lain pulang."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "They rode on, but their food had run out in a year of drought. By the road stood the two tents of Umm Ma‘bad, a woman who gave water and food to those who passed. They asked to buy meat and dates, but she had none."
msgstr "Mereka meneruskan perjalanan, tetapi bekalan makanan mereka telah habis dalam tahun kemarau. Di tepi jalan terdapat dua khemah milik Umm Ma‘bad, seorang wanita yang memberi air dan makanan kepada para musafir. Mereka meminta untuk membeli daging dan kurma, tetapi dia tidak memilikinya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Hungry and far from home, they stopped at the tent of Umm Ma‘bad. She had no food to give them."
msgstr "Dalam keadaan lapar dan jauh dari rumah, mereka berhenti di khemah Umm Ma‘bad. Dia tidak mempunyai makanan untuk diberikan kepada mereka."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At the back of her tent stood a ewe too weak to follow the flock. The Prophet ﷺ passed his hand over her udder, spoke the name of Allah, and milked until froth rose over the vessel. Umm Ma‘bad drank first, he drank last."
msgstr "Di belakang khemahnya ada seekor biri-biri betina yang terlalu lemah untuk mengikuti kawanannya. Rasulullah ﷺ mengusap ambingnya, menyebut nama Allah, lalu memerah susunya sehingga buih melimpah di atas bekas. Umm Ma‘bad minum dahulu, manakala baginda minum terakhir."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Her thin sheep had no milk. The Prophet ﷺ said Allah’s name and milked her, and everyone drank!"
msgstr "Biri-birinya yang kurus tidak mengeluarkan susu. Rasulullah ﷺ menyebut nama Allah lalu memerah susunya, dan semua orang dapat minum!"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "When her husband came home, she described their guest: a man of shining beauty, his words like beads slipping from a string. “By Allah,” said Abu Ma‘bad, “that is the man from Quraysh.”"
msgstr "Apabila suaminya pulang, dia menceritakan tentang tetamu mereka: seorang lelaki yang tampan berseri, tutur katanya seperti manik-manik yang meluncur dari seutas tali. “Demi Allah,” kata Abu Ma‘bad, “itulah lelaki dari Quraysh.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "When her husband came home, she told him about their guest: a shining face, and words like beads on a string."
msgstr "Apabila suaminya pulang, dia menceritakan tentang tetamu mereka: wajah yang berseri dan tutur kata seperti manik-manik yang tersusun pada seutas tali."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Each morning the Muslims of Madinah watched for him till the heat drove them in. Then a man on a fort saw the travellers in white, shimmering in the mirage: “Here is your good fortune, the one you have been waiting for!”"
msgstr "Setiap pagi, umat Islam di Madinah menunggu kedatangannya sehingga bahang panas memaksa mereka masuk semula. Kemudian, seorang lelaki di atas kubu melihat para musafir berpakaian putih berkilauan dalam bayangan fatamorgana. “Inilah keberuntungan kalian—orang yang selama ini kalian nantikan!”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "In Madinah, people waited every morning in the hot sun. At last a man shouted: he is here!"
msgstr "Di Madinah, orang ramai menunggu setiap pagi di bawah terik matahari. Akhirnya, seorang lelaki menjerit: “Dia sudah tiba!”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "They found him at Quba, in the shade of a palm with Abu Bakr. Most had never seen him, and they greeted Abu Bakr. Then the sun fell on the Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr held his cloak over him, and at that they knew him."
msgstr "Mereka menemuinya di Quba, berteduh di bawah pokok kurma bersama Abu Bakr. Kebanyakan mereka belum pernah melihatnya, lalu menyambut Abu Bakr. Kemudian, cahaya matahari menyinari Rasulullah ﷺ, dan Abu Bakr memayunginya dengan jubah. Ketika itulah mereka mengenalinya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "They found him resting in the shade of a palm tree at Quba, with Abu Bakr beside him."
msgstr "Mereka menemuinya sedang berehat di bawah teduhan pokok kurma di Quba, dengan Abu Bakr di sisinya."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "There ‘Ali caught up with him, after three days in Makkah returning what people had left in the Prophet’s ﷺ care. The Prophet ﷺ founded his mosque at Quba and prayed in it, and on a Friday he rode on towards Madinah."
msgstr "Di sana, ‘Ali menyusulnya selepas tiga hari di Makkah untuk memulangkan barang-barang yang diamanahkan orang kepada Rasulullah ﷺ. Rasulullah ﷺ membina masjidnya di Quba dan menunaikan solat di situ. Pada hari Jumaat, baginda menunggang menuju Madinah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At Quba he built a mosque and prayed in it. Then he rode on into Madinah."
msgstr "Di Quba, baginda membina sebuah masjid dan menunaikan solat di dalamnya. Kemudian, baginda meneruskan perjalanan dengan menunggang ke Madinah."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "On the way he prayed his first Friday prayer in Madinah. Clan after clan came out: “Stay with us. We have the numbers and the strength.” Each time he said of his camel, “Let her go her way; she is under orders.”"
msgstr "Dalam perjalanan, baginda menunaikan solat Jumaat pertamanya di Madinah. Kabilah demi kabilah keluar menyambutnya: “Tinggallah bersama kami. Kami ramai dan kuat.” Setiap kali, baginda berkata tentang untanya, “Biarkan dia meneruskan jalannya; dia sedang mengikut arahan.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "At last the Prophet ﷺ rode into Madinah. Family after family asked him to stay, but he let his camel walk on."
msgstr "Akhirnya, Rasulullah ﷺ menunggang masuk ke Madinah. Keluarga demi keluarga memintanya tinggal bersama mereka, tetapi baginda membiarkan untanya terus berjalan."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "The whole town poured out, and women on the rooftops strained to see: “Which one is he?” At last the camel knelt in a yard where dates were laid to dry. “This, if Allah wills, is the stopping place,” he said."
msgstr "Seluruh penduduk keluar beramai-ramai, sementara para wanita di atas bumbung menjenguk untuk melihat: “Yang manakah orangnya?” Akhirnya, unta itu berlutut di sebuah halaman tempat kurma dijemur. “Di sinilah tempat persinggahan, insya-Allah,” kata baginda."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Children ran and people climbed up high to see him. His camel knelt in a yard where dates were dried."
msgstr "Kanak-kanak berlari dan orang ramai naik ke tempat tinggi untuk melihat baginda. Untanya berlutut di sebuah halaman tempat kurma dijemur."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "There his mosque rose, from bricks of sun-dried clay. The Prophet ﷺ carried them with the others, chanting, “O Allah, there is no good but the good of the Hereafter, so help the Ansar and the Emigrants.”"
msgstr "Di sana masjidnya dibina daripada batu bata tanah liat yang dijemur hingga kering. Nabi ﷺ mengangkat batu bata bersama yang lain sambil melantunkan, “Ya Allah, tiada kebaikan selain kebaikan akhirat. Maka bantulah kaum Ansar dan kaum Muhajirin.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "There they built a mosque, and the Prophet ﷺ carried bricks to help."
msgstr "Di sana mereka membina sebuah masjid, dan Nabi ﷺ turut mengangkat batu bata untuk membantu."

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "Then the fever of Madinah laid his companions low. Makkah had been the dearest of lands to him, and now he prayed for their new home: “O Allah, make Madinah dear to us as You made Makkah dear to us, or dearer.”"
msgstr "Kemudian demam Madinah membuat para sahabatnya jatuh sakit. Makkah ialah negeri yang paling dicintainya, dan kini baginda berdoa untuk tempat tinggal baharu mereka: “Ya Allah, jadikan Madinah kami cintai sebagaimana Engkau menjadikan Makkah kami cintai, bahkan lebih lagi.”"

#: src/content/text.generated.js
msgid "He prayed that Allah would make Madinah as dear to them as Makkah, and even dearer."
msgstr "Baginda berdoa agar Allah menjadikan Madinah sama dicintai mereka seperti Makkah, bahkan lebih lagi."

